<br/>
<b>IMPORTANT:</b> The gear recommendations below are simply that; recommendations. With the addition of reforging in Cataclysm, you will often have to change around pieces of gear in order to fix stat caps, such as balancing hit and expertise caps. You will often find that certain pieces may not have a role until another piece is obtained. As a general rule, higher item level pieces will almost always win out - remember that extra hit and expertise can be replaced, but Strength <i>cannot</i> be reforged into.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="body-armor">Body Armor for Fury Warrior DPS</h3>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="head-for-fury-warrior-dps">Head for Fury Warrior DPS</h4>With the new Inferno Rune Dungeons, our best helmet is now the T11 helm we can acquire from the new currency.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=59359/reinforced-bio-optic-killshades">
<img alt="Reinforced Bio-Optic Killshades" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gizmo_newgoggles.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Bio-Optic Killshades</span></a> is far ahead of the other options - the increase item level means extra stats, and the ability to customize which stats you can put into it means we can fill some useful caps with it, or simply gain extra Critical Strike Rating<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Helm Enchant</b>: <a class="q7 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62368/arcanum-of-the-dragonmaw">
